\nabla_\mu J^\mu_{\text{causal}} = 0,
\end{equation}
is computed at horizon-grade resolution and transmitted to APOLLO-CM as a
boundary condition on all tensor evolution. The invariant constrains:

\begin{itemize}
    \item permissible curvature evolution,
    \item allowed nuclear-to-relativistic transitions,
    \item chronological ordering of metric updates,
    \item tensor field admissibility under extreme forcing.
\end{itemize}

These constraints ensure that APOLLO-CM evolves only within the causal domain
defined by APSE-v9.

